        <p>Lort Coutteney, Local Government - ln-s—pe. titer, opeu"! inquiry at Newton Abbo7. on Thursday, into grave CO ' plaints which have been brought against the manaVv, ' merit of the heal we.,rktiouse. VVitnesses -.vere calh d aalt. " deposed that the" jumper," a sort of sack, used for Por',.„ poses similar to that of the sirait waistcoat, was in stant use in the workhouse, and that aced inmates bad been placed in it naked and then tied to the irons of till , bedsteads. A Mr. Bovey (lied five days after conflpe— ment in the " jumper," and she was actually tled down within a few hours of her death. Other , witnerscs alleged that the wards of the workhourr ' were in a filthy condition, and many of the innaate9 infested w.th vermin. A nurse. Alice Hinton. wearer 4 the bronze modal of the Workhouse Nurdog Association., , whia joined the staff of the Newton Workhouse, December 28th last, deposed to many of tho foregonl.g. facts. Ouc intnate, named Nirs. .Nielralls, the nurse she found apparently dying. The woman wae ver,7 dirty and covered with vermin. Her hair had been cos,,-• ' off and her toie nails were lik- claws, b•i•ire,r two anda,,,, half inches long. The sanitary arrangements in Bowe ot the wards were filthy. Aftither woman who wail'''' para!yrld had her finger . nails so long that the, _ had made wounds in her flesh. In passing through '1 the yard, the nurse sa4l sne saw an . idiot vrorna,. ' crouched in a corner with her face bruised. The go ..'. darts had built a shed for her in the 'var.), and Witner:': liai noticed that the toss threw stora,s arid snowballSa' i.er. When the master's son was at home he was ring'elder. .Tho °boys raid that thew Pelted the olu •' wean to make her swear. The witness alleged thilt . the matron neglected her duties, and that during I" i three months she (witnels) remained at the Workhousr 1 the matron was only five times in the sick ward to .bc,r 1 knowledge. It was further iillec,,d that the fighto4. A among the idkits was especially drcalful on mornings, when the matron wRs in bed, and Nur Hinton added;that she had also c(implained to the mat," • , A of immorality that was going on amono..st thrt innlateS,; 1 The inquiry was adjourned. It is wzpected tn laSt '.; week, as there are upwards of 60 witnesses to lit' called.</p>
