        <p>• A PENNY SAVED IS A PENNY MADE. How to save money. Waste not. want not. Don't furnish on the hire system, with its extravagant high prices, arbitrary agreements, and despotic restrictions. For instance. suppose A furnishes for £lOO on the hire system with B and pas B £99 in instalmeuts. /mt. neglects to pay B the last instalment in time, the agreement gives B the paver to forcibly retake possession of the furniture, but the whole of the £9g paid is then forfeited to -B, consequently B gets both money and goods. In adlition to the ab,ve disadvantages the price charged is exhorbitant, often 200 and 30) per cent more than for cash at a proper edablistiment. it is high time this system was de lard illegal. Be it known that at Worsley's " The Itantheon,"Gaythorn, Manchester, high-class New and Second-hand Furniture may 1), had at the exact advertised marked cash price, 110 less under a, y circumstances. Also. that in cases where it is inconvenient ti pay the whale of the money down. Worsley's are prepared to assist purchasers by allowing the aecouot to be aid at convenient intervals. charging only a small percentage for the. privilege. By this means the purchaser knows exactly whet he is charged for the goods. and escapes all fear and trembling as to the loss of his furniture if he happens to miss a payment. Worsley's have on view complete Hoose.s of Furniture for £l5, £2O, £25, £32 10s.. and £45 up to £l,OOO. full particulars of which are supplied on application post. free. "the Pantheon is packed from floor to ceiling with countless bargains in Dining. Draw- ing. Sitting, ,nd Bcdroom ,Furniture, Office and Library Furniture, by Lamb, Gi/lows, (teen, Garnett, &amp;c. Read the following sample bargains High-class Second-hand Dining. room :Furniture, consisting of a massive suite of nine pieces, six heavy carved single chairs, large comfortable couch, and a pair of luxurious upholstelied easy chairs, by Henry Ogden and Sons ; cost £75; price for quick sale. £2